&lt;p&amp;gt;Net Intake Rate is the number of new entrants to the first grade (of primary or secondary level) who are of official school-entrance age, expressed as a percentage of the population of the corresponding age. The 2019 baseline was revised in 2022 (DPF3) and then recalibrated in 2023 to allow comparison with baseline and actual data since: (i) a new population and housing census took place in 2022/23 showing an inter-censal annual growth rate of 2.3% between 2012 and 2022 and leading to a revision of the underlying population estimates; (ii) a change in official government policy required children to start primary and secondary school at a younger age (revised from 7 to 6 for Grade 1 and age 13 to 12 for Grade 7); and (iii) the academic cycle changed (from a January to December cycle to September to August). To ensure a like-for-like comparison across the project cycle, the data applies a consistent census projection for the baseline and end line, pooled.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&amp;gt;

